  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "1U8RdHRH88032Of1ogSr1efSfIs=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:28.507Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## No invite code needed\n\nThe hosted Vetra Studio is gated behind an early-access code, but the same agent ships as a CLI you run yourself. The trade is the API key: locally you bring your own **Anthropic API key**, because the agent runs on Claude. Prerequisites are Node \u2265 24 on macOS or Linux; pnpm is optional (the installer uses it if present, offers to install it, else falls back to npm).\n\nTwo install paths:\n\n```bash\n# A \u2014 installer script (sets up both the `ph` and `vetra` CLIs)\ncurl -fsSL https://get.vetra.io | sh\n\n# B \u2014 straight from the Vetra registry, nothing piped to a shell\nnpm install -g ph-cmd vetra-cli --registry=https://registry.vetra.io\npnpm add -g ph-cmd vetra-cli --registry=https://registry.vetra.io\n```\n\nIf you want to read the script first, `curl -fsSL https://get.vetra.io -o install-vetra.sh`, inspect, then `sh install-vetra.sh`. The first launch walks Claude auth, then prints the Studio URL \u2014 open `http://localhost:8090/`. Re-start any time with `vetra`.\n\nFrom source: clone `powerhouse-inc/vetra-cli`, `pnpm install`, `pnpm dev` for the interactive agent REPL with an embedded Reactor and Switchboard, exporting `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...` once. When the agent starts a build the logs print `Vetra Studio: http://localhost:8090/d/<driveId>`. `pnpm dev:reset` wipes the local dev workspace.\n\n## Three ports, no fallback\n\nA single `vetra` process runs the REPL plus an embedded Reactor and Switchboard, and it reserves three ports **with no fallback** \u2014 free them first or startup fails:\n\n| Service | Port | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Vetra Studio (proxy) | 8090 | Browser entry point, the URL you open |\n| Connect | 27370 | Editor front-end |\n| Switchboard | 59220 | GraphQL API |\n\nThese are deliberately unusual numbers so they do not collide with the ordinary Powerhouse dev ports \u2014 `ph vetra` puts Connect on 3001 and Switchboard on 4001, and `ph connect studio` uses 3000. Running `vetra` and `ph vetra` side by side is therefore fine.\n\n_Source: `apps/academy/docs/academy/01-GetStarted/00-VetraStudio.md` (Running Vetra Studio locally), Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:37:27.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:28.507Z"
    }
  },
